        "t2": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABQlcGMg",
            "number": 1669,
            "title": "fix(types): emit declarations that typecheck with skipLibCheck: false",
            "body": "Fixes #1657\n\n### Summary\n\nDownstream TypeScript projects importing `h3` with `skipLibCheck: false` failed `tsc --noEmit` unless they targeted `ESNext` and installed the optional peer dependency `crossws`:\n\n1. `dist/h3.d.mts` emitted `static override isError` on `HTTPError`. Because `Error.isError` only exists in the `ESNext` lib, consumers targeting `ES2022` (or any pre-`ESNext` lib) got `TS4113`.\n2. `dist/index.d.mts` imported `Hooks`, `Peer`, and `Message` from the optional peer `crossws`, producing `TS2307` when `crossws` is not installed.\n\n### Changes\n\n- Updated `build.config.ts` (`hooks.end`) to post-process emitted `dist/**/*.d.mts`:\n  - Strip `override` from `static override isError` in published declarations while keeping `static override isError` in `src/error.ts` so this repo's own `noImplicitOverride` + `ESNext` typecheck continues to pass (`override` on `name` and `cause` stays intact because both exist in `ES2022`).\n  - Prepend `// @ts-ignore optional peer dependency` above the `from \"crossws\"` import in `dist/index.d.mts`, suppressing `TS2307` when `crossws` is absent while preserving exact nominal types (`Peer`, `Message`, `Hooks`) when `crossws` is installed.\n- Added a real `tsc --noEmit` consumer regression suite in `test/dts-consumer.test.ts` testing `skipLibCheck: false` + `noImplicitOverride: true` across `ES2022` and `ESNext`, both with and without `crossws` installed (and asserting nominal equality when `crossws` is present).\n\n### Verification\n\n- **Red before fix:** `pnpm exec vitest --run test/dts-consumer.test.ts` reproduced both `TS4113` (`h3.d.mts`) and `TS2307` (`index.d.mts`) on `ES2022` without `crossws`.\n- **Green after fix:**\n  - `pnpm build`\n  - `pnpm lint` (`oxlint` + `oxfmt --check`)\n  - `pnpm typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`)\n  - `pnpm exec vitest --run test/dts-consumer.test.ts` — 4/4 passed.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved TypeScript compatibility for package declarations in downstream projects using ES2022 or ESNext, including setups with or without optional WebSocket support.\n  * Corrected declaration compatibility for `HTTPError.isError`, helping consumers compile with strict library checking enabled.\n  * These updates make it easier to use the package’s public types across different TypeScript configurations and optional dependency setups.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
